AEM Content Fragments

What is a Content Fragment?

A Content Fragment is a reusable, structured piece of content in Adobe Experience Manager (AEM). It is independent of webpage design and can be reused across multiple channels.

Content Fragment Model

A Content Fragment Model defines the structure and fields of a Content Fragment.

Examples of Data Types

- Single Line Text
- Multi Line Text
- Number
- Boolean
- Date and Time
- Enumeration
- Content Reference
- Fragment Reference

Content Fragment vs Experience Fragment

Content Fragment| Experience Fragment
Structured content| Content with layout
No webpage design| Includes design and components
Content-focused| Experience-focused
Reusable across channels| Reusable page experience

Working Process

1. Create a Content Fragment Model.
2. Define fields and data types.
3. Enable the model.
4. Create a Content Fragment.
5. Add content.
6. Publish and reuse it.

Advantages

- Content reusability
- Easy maintenance
- Multi-channel delivery
- Reduced duplication
- Supports headless CMS

Real-Time Example

In an e-commerce application, product details can be stored in a Content Fragment and reused on websites and mobile applications.

Conclusion

Content Fragments help developers and content authors manage structured content independently of webpage presentation.
